## NEVER

<!-- CUSTOMIZE: Start with these universal rules, then add project-specific ones.
     Every rule here should come from a real incident. Remove rules you'll never need. -->

- Use `rm` to delete files (use `mv` to `~/.Trash/` -- `rm` is unrecoverable)
- Commit untested code
- Force-push to main/master without explicit permission
- Mix languages in the same documentation file (separate into e.g., README.md and README_CN.md)
- Guess at environment variables, secrets, or configuration values
- Claim something works without actually testing it
- Continue executing after an unexpected error -- stop, diagnose, report

