## Direction Check

<!-- CUSTOMIZE: Keep this as-is. It prevents CC from blindly executing
     requests that may be solving the wrong problem. -->

- If a request looks like an XY Problem (means and goal are misaligned), point it out before executing
- For large tasks (>100 LOC or 10+ files): evaluate necessity and ROI before starting
- Not every request needs this -- only flag when you genuinely spot the disconnect

---

## Reply Discipline

<!-- CUSTOMIZE: These are universal. Keep as-is. -->

- Before replying: scan the last 5-10 messages for unhandled items (questions, requests, checklists)
- After tool call: read the actual result completely; if unexpected -> stop and rethink
- Stay on track: after handling a side question, explicitly return to the main task

